      "html": "<div class=\"ds-notice\" role=\"alert\">Unknown variables will send blank: subject, position.</div>",
      "css": ".ds-notice{padding:.5rem .75rem;border:1px solid var(--danger-line);border-radius:.5rem;background:var(--danger-soft);color:var(--danger);font-size:.75rem;line-height:1.125rem}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Send Constellation",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "send-sky",
      "description": "The signature: one star per recipient, grouped by batch, igniting gold or rose from the live send log. Stays Night in both modes.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-sky\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"ds-batch\"><svg class=\"ds-line\"><polyline points=\"10,24 40,40 70,14 100,34\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"rgb(255 255 255 / .22)\"/></svg><i class=\"ds-star ds-sent\" style=\"left:0;top:14px\"></i><i class=\"ds-star ds-sent\" style=\"left:30px;top:30px\"></i><i class=\"ds-star ds-failed\" style=\"left:60px;top:4px\"></i><i class=\"ds-star ds-sent\" style=\"left:90px;top:24px\"></i></span><span class=\"ds-batch ds-batch-2\"><svg class=\"ds-line\"><polyline points=\"10,40 40,14 70,34\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"rgb(255 255 255 / .22)\"/></svg><i class=\"ds-star ds-now\" style=\"left:0;top:30px\"></i><i class=\"ds-star ds-now\" style=\"left:30px;top:4px\"></i><i class=\"ds-star\" style=\"left:60px;top:24px\"></i></span></div>",
      "css": ".ds-sky{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:center;gap:.75rem 1.75rem;padding:1rem;border-radius:.75rem;background:#1a0a30}.ds-batch{position:relative;width:110px;height:3.125rem}.ds-batch-2{width:80px}.ds-line{position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;overflow:visible}.ds-star{position:absolute;width:1.25rem;height:1.25rem;border-radius:50%;background:radial-gradient(circle,#9d8fc7 0 16%,#1a0a30 30%)}.ds-now{background:radial-gradient(circle,#fff 0 18%,#1a0a30 36%);animation:ds-pulse 1.1s ease-in-out infinite alternate}.ds-sent{background:radial-gradient(circle,#fff 0 16%,#ffd98a 28%,#ffd98a00 68%),#1a0a30;animation:ds-ignite 560ms cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1) both}.ds-failed{background:radial-gradient(circle,#ffd5de 0 14%,#ff5c7f 28%,#ff5c7f00 68%),#1a0a30;animation:ds-ignite 560ms cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1) both}@keyframes ds-pulse{from{opacity:.45}}@keyframes ds-ignite{0%{opacity:.35;transform:scale(.5)}55%{opacity:1;transform:scale(1.35)}100%{opacity:1;transform:scale(1)}}@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-star{animation:none}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Every Recipient Is a Star",
    "overview": "BatchMail is a working tool under a night sky. A deep aubergine sky drifts behind solid violet-tinted cards, and the sky stays behind the task until a batch goes out. Then the one signature moment arrives: each recipient is a star, grouped into small constellations by batch, and each star lights as its email leaves. Gold means it went out. Rose means it did not.\n\nThe theme lives in the world, not on the controls. Buttons, inputs, tabs, and tables stay standard and legible, set in Geist, on opaque surfaces at a compact working density. The system refuses a glassy dark dashboard with neon edges, and it refuses space costume on the controls.\n\nDark is the default. The server renders the dark class on the root element, a script that runs before paint removes it when `batchmail_dark` is saved as `0` in localStorage, and the header toggle writes that key. Light mode is the same world at dawn: a lavender sky, white cards, the same deep violet header. Motion has three speeds. The sky moves on transform and opacity alone, over 70 to 720 seconds, with a 7 to 9 second twinkle. Interface transitions run 150 to 280ms. Completion runs longer: the rail connector and the progress bar fill over 420ms, and ignite takes 520 to 700ms. All of this CSS motion stops under prefers-reduced-motion, where the sky holds still and the interface changes state without travel.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Dark by default, with a lavender light mode behind one toggle.",
      "A living sky behind opaque working surfaces.",
      "One saturated ultraviolet for action, one gold for done, one rose for failure.",
      "Geist throughout, Geist Mono for code, variables, and logs.",
      "Email surfaces stay as recipients will see them, outside the theme."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Starlight Rule",
        "body": "Gold means done or delivered. Primary actions, hover states, highlights, and warnings never use it, so a gold mark always means work is finished.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Equal Failure Rule",
        "body": "A failed recipient gets the same star size, the same ignite, and a place in the same bar as a delivered one, in rose. Failures are never quieter than successes.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Recipient's View Rule",
        "body": "The email editor and preview show the message as recipients will see it, so they stay light in dark mode and take no theme color. Outgoing templates are not part of this design system.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Literal Mono Rule",
        "body": "Mono appears only on text that is literally data or code. It is never decoration.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Clear Title Rule",
        "body": "The star layers are masked out of the top 10.5rem of the content column, so no star reads as punctuation beside the title.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Solid Surface Rule",
        "body": "Working surfaces are opaque, so text contrast never depends on where a star happens to drift. No backdrop blur and no glass.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do reserve Starlight Gold for finished steps and delivered email, with Star Ink on any gold fill.",
      "Do show every failure in Failure Rose beside a count or message that stays findable after the run.",
      "Do keep working surfaces opaque, with the sky visible only in the gaps between them.",
      "Do animate the sky with transform and opacity only, and keep interface transitions within 150 to 280ms.",
      "Do gate every new animation, including scripted scrolling, so it stops under prefers-reduced-motion.",
      "Do define new colors as a dark and light pair in both theme blocks.",
      "Do keep the CNCP logo on a Header Violet chip in light mode, because it is white with a cyan glow and washes out on light grounds, and keep the name \"Cisco NetConnect PUP · Manila\" in the header."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use glass, backdrop blur, or glowing borders on the interface. The only glow in the system belongs to send stars.",
      "Don't dress controls as space objects. Buttons, inputs, tabs, and tables stay standard, and the theme stays in the sky and the constellation.",
      "Don't use gold for primary actions, hover states, or warnings.",
      "Don't theme the email editor or preview, or apply these tokens to outgoing templates.",
      "Don't let stars drift behind the page title block.",
      "Don't add planets or orbits to the working app. They belong to sign-in."
    ]
  }
}
